index d532f62..4f255d3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,14 +3,34 @@
 A small command-line task tracker that stores tasks in a JSON file.
 
 ```
-tasker add [-p N] <title words...>     add a task (priority 1-5, default 3)
-tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority] list open tasks (or all)
+tasker add [-p N] [--tag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD] <title words...>
+                                                  add a task (priority 1-5, default 3;
+                                                  --tag is repeatable)
+tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority|due] [--tag T] [--overdue]
+                                                  list open tasks (or all)
 tasker done <id>                        mark a task done
 tasker rm <id>                          delete a task
-tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T]     change priority or title
+tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T] [--tag T] [--untag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD|none]
+                                                  change priority, title, tags or due date
+tasker tags                             print every tag used by open tasks with its count
 ```
 
+Notes:
+
+- Tags are normalised on save: trimmed, lower-cased, de-duplicated and sorted.
+  They must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` (e.g. `home`, `work-2`).
+- Due dates are `YYYY-MM-DD` and stored as UTC midnight. `--due none` on
+  `edit` clears the due date.
+- `list --overdue` shows open tasks whose due date is strictly before today.
+- `list --tag T` (repeatable) keeps only tasks having ALL given tags.
+- `list --sort due` orders by due date ascending; tasks without a due date
+  come last, ties broken by ID.
+- `FormatTask` appends ` (due YYYY-MM-DD)` and ` [tag1,tag2]` when present:
+  `#4 [ ] P2 file taxes (due 2026-04-15) [home,money]`.
+
 The data file is `$TASKER_FILE` (default `tasks.json` in the current directory).
+It uses schema version 2; version-1 files still load (tasks simply have no
+tags or due dates).
 
 ## Layout
 - `internal/model` — the Task type and validation.
